   "l": "Washing and sweeping the dark viewing —\ncan you be without a flaw?",
   "v": true,
   "i": "Scour the dark mirror clean — can you leave it without a blemish?",
   "n": "玄覽 is two words, not one: 'dark' before 'viewing', a modifier and its noun, as 常道 was in chapter 1. The Mawangdui manuscripts are read as writing 監 here, an old spelling of 鑑 'mirror' — which turns the phrase into 'the dark mirror', and washing a blemish off a mirror makes plainer sense than washing one off a vision. The received text has 覽 and we keep it; the idiomatic line follows the mirror, and you should know that is a choice. 疵 is a flaw in a stone, not a moral fault."
  },
