   "l": "Heaven's gate opening and shutting —\ncan you play the female?",
   "v": true,
   "i": "The gate of heaven opens and closes — can you take the female part?",
   "n": "天門 is 'heaven's gate' — a modifier and its noun, not a compound word; 門 is the same gate that ended chapter 1. What opens and shuts is left unsaid: the commentators take it of heaven's own working, and of the breath going in and out of a body. 雌 is concrete — the hen, the female bird — not an abstraction, and it is this book's standing figure for the side that yields and outlasts. 為 is read wéi, 'to do, to act as'; read wèi it would mean 'for the sake of'."
